  "stem": "In the \\(xy\\)-plane, the graph of \\(2x - 5y = c\\), where \\(c\\) is a constant, passes through the point \\((-4, 2)\\). What is the value of \\(c\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "mcq",
  "choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(18\\)",
    "C": "\\(-18\\)",
    "D": "\\(-8\\)"
  },
  "answer": "C",
  "spr_answers": null,
  "solution": [
    "Substitute \\(x = -4\\) and \\(y = 2\\): \\(2(-4) - 5(2) = c\\).",
    "So \\(c = -8 - 10 = -18\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": {
    "A": "Incorrect. This is \\(-8 + 10\\); the term \\(-5y\\) was added instead of subtracted.",
    "B": "Incorrect. The sum is \\(-8 - 10 = -18\\), not \\(18\\).",
    "C": "Correct. \\(2(-4) - 5(2) = -8 - 10 = -18\\).",
    "D": "Incorrect. This is only \\(2x\\); the \\(-5y\\) term was left out."
  },
  "traps": {
    "A": "sign_error",
    "B": "arithmetic",
    "D": "stopped_early"
  },
